+TB_COMMIT="$(materialize_recovery_source "$PM_REPO" "$TB_SOURCE" "$TB_VERSION")"
+AI_COMMIT="$(materialize_recovery_source "$AI_REPO" "$AI_SOURCE" "$AI_VERSION")"
+
+# task-board and tb-sessiond ship from one repository and share one recovery
+# source worktree. A divergent reported commit means the installed pair is not
+# coherent, and it blocks Step 2 rather than picking one of the two.
+test "$(extract_reported_commit "$SESSIOND_VERSION")" \
+  = "$(extract_reported_commit "$TB_VERSION")"
+
+printf 'skill-project-management=%s\nrelux-agents-infra=%s\n' \
+  "$TB_COMMIT" "$AI_COMMIT" > "$RECOVERY_ROOT/recovery-source-commits.txt"
+{
+  require_saved_binary_source_identity task-board "$TB_SOURCE" "$TB_VERSION"
+  require_saved_binary_source_identity tb-sessiond "$TB_SOURCE" \
+    "$SESSIOND_VERSION"
+  require_saved_binary_source_identity agents-infra "$AI_SOURCE" "$AI_VERSION"
+} > "$RECOVERY_ROOT/binary-source-identities.txt"
+```
+
+Parse failure, an unknown commit, dirty detached source, a binary/source OID
+mismatch, a failed `cmp`, or any missing executable blocks Step 2. It is never
+treated as an absent identity or a usable rollback baseline.
+
+**Property of this plan: the recovery baseline and the recovery binary are the
+same pair by construction, not by a maintained literal.** Each source worktree
+is created at the commit its own saved executable reports, resolved in the
+owning repository at execution time. There is no revision written into this
+document that has to be refreshed when either repository moves, and no
+execution can silently pair a newer binary with an older source. If an
+executable's version output cannot be parsed to a commit, or that commit does
+not resolve in the repository, `materialize_recovery_source` refuses and no
+baseline is produced — the plan reports `unknown` and stops rather than
+guessing a nearby revision. `require_saved_binary_source_identity` therefore
+becomes a tautology guard that still catches a concurrent repository mutation
+or a tampered worktree between materialization and use.
+
+For the bridge snapshot, use a fresh
+`$HOME/.local/state/TASK-260830-s5ro4e/bridge-pair`. The same derivation
+applies unchanged: the saved `0.25.0` and `v1.7.0` executables name their own
+commits, and the exact tags are asserted against the resolved OIDs rather than
+substituted for them. Never overwrite a prior snapshot.
+
+Reusable same-filesystem binary restore:
+
+```bash
+restore_binary() {
+  name="$1"
+  source="$RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/$name"
+  destination="$HOME/.local/bin/$name"
+  temporary="$HOME/.local/bin/.$name.rollback.$$"
+  test -f "$source"
+  test ! -L "$source"
+  install -m 0755 "$source" "$temporary"
+  mv -f "$temporary" "$destination"
+}
+```
+
+Coherent task-board skill/role restore, executed only for the release-owned
+paths listed above:
+
+```bash
+restore_project_management_surface() {
+  PM_SKILLS="$HOME/.agents/skills"
+  PM_STAGE="$PM_SKILLS/.project-management.rollback.$$"
+  rsync -a --delete "$RECOVERY_ROOT/pm/project-management-skill/" "$PM_STAGE/"
+  mv "$PM_SKILLS/project-management" "$PM_SKILLS/.project-management.failed.$$"
+  mv "$PM_STAGE" "$PM_SKILLS/project-management"
+  test -L "$HOME/.claude/skills/project-management"
+  test -L "$HOME/.codex/skills/project-management"
+  ln -sfn "$PM_SKILLS/project-management" "$HOME/.claude/skills/project-management"
+  ln -sfn "$PM_SKILLS/project-management" "$HOME/.codex/skills/project-management"
+
+  for role in context-builder coordinator developer doc-writer orchestrator \
+    researcher reviewer solution-architect tester; do
+    stage="$HOME/.roles/.$role.rollback.$$"
+    rsync -a --delete "$RECOVERY_ROOT/pm/roles/$role/" "$stage/"
+    mv "$HOME/.roles/$role" "$HOME/.roles/.$role.failed.$$"
+    mv "$stage" "$HOME/.roles/$role"
+  done
+
+  install -m 0644 "$RECOVERY_ROOT/pm/install.json" \
+    "$HOME/.config/task-board/.install.json.rollback.$$"
+  mv -f "$HOME/.config/task-board/.install.json.rollback.$$" \
+    "$HOME/.config/task-board/install.json"
+}
+```
+
+Coherent agents-infra managed-runtime restore uses the saved old executable and
+exact old source. It deliberately does not copy `~/.agents` wholesale and does
+not print config contents:
+
+```bash
+restore_agents_infra_surface() {
+  restore_binary agents-infra
+  restore_binary model-harness
+  "$RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/agents-infra" setup global \
+    --source-dir "$RECOVERY_ROOT/sources/relux-agents-infra"
+  "$RECOVERY_ROOT/bin/agents-infra" verify global
+}
+```
+
+Each rollback block below runs in one `set -euo pipefail` shell after defining
+the three primitives exactly as written above. A partial primitive invocation
+is a rollback failure, not a successful half-restore.
+
+All restore procedures in this plan are **UNTESTED operationally** until a
+release operator rehearses them on a disposable home/runtime and records the
+real exits. They are not assumed reversible.
+
+## Release order
+
+### Step 0 — freeze the current working pair
+
+Repository/version: whatever pair is actually installed when this step runs.
+The operator does not read a version out of this document. The snapshot block
+above reads `task-board --version`, `tb-sessiond --version` and
+`agents-infra version` from the *saved* executables and materializes each
+recovery source at the commit those executables report.
+
+At the time this plan was written the installed pair measured
+`0.24.3-172-g063197b1` embedding `v0.2.0` and `v1.6.1-103-g4270549`. That is
+recorded as an observation, not as a pin: both repositories moved during this
+planning task alone, so any literal here is expected to be stale by the time
+the migration runs, and nothing in the procedure depends on these values.
+
+Required board capability: run read, preflight, one real spawn, outcome
+resource handoff and reviewer route using the installed pair, then capture the
+`current-pair` recovery snapshot above. The snapshot is admissible only when
+its task-board, tb-sessiond and agents-infra version outputs each resolve to the
+HEAD of their saved clean detached source tree. In a disposable HOME, the saved
+agents-infra binary must run `setup global --source-dir` against the source
+worktree derived from that same binary and then `verify global`, both with exit
+zero. An installed executable whose reported commit does not resolve in its
+repository blocks Step 0; the operator repairs or reinstalls a resolvable pair
+rather than substituting a nearby revision.
+
+In-flight runs: remain on their existing process images. Do not restart or
+kill them. Do not begin Step 2 while a run is at a handoff/acceptance mutation
+boundary.
+
+Mismatch window: none; this step only copies explicitly named non-secret
+artifacts and creates detached source worktrees.
+
+Rollback command: no installed artifact changes. On snapshot failure, stop and
+discard only the newly created task-scoped snapshot after inspecting it; no
+release step may start.
+
+Rollback status: **UNTESTED**.
